[2026-07-30 08:16:21,501 - Orcar.agent - INFO] conclusion="<Observation>\nThe search results strongly indicate the regression is in Django's choice-display helper injection. Field.contribute_to_class() unconditionally assigns get_<field>_display on the model class using setattr(..., partialmethod(cls._get_FIELD_display, field=self)), so a user-defined get_foo_bar_display() can be shadowed in Django 2.2+. ModelBase.__new__() confirms this happens during class construction, and Model._get_FIELD_display() is only the underlying formatter, not the source of override precedence.\n</Observation>" bug_locations=[BugLocations(file_path='django/db/models/fields/__init__.py', class_name='Field', method_name='contribute_to_class'), BugLocations(file_path='django/db/models/base.py', class_name='ModelBase', method_name='__new__'), BugLocations(file_path='django/db/models/base.py', class_name='Model', method_name='_get_FIELD_display')]
